" Spec [Chords][[Editing]]: <Ctrl-A>/<Ctrl-X> (songwriter#chord#TransposeChord)
" transpose the chord under the cursor by their count of semitones; off a chord
" they are Vim's own increment/decrement.

Given (transpose chord up chromatically):
               Am7

Execute (transpose chord up chromatically):
  call cursor(1, 14)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
               A#m7

Given (transpose chord down chromatically):
               Am7

Execute (transpose chord down chromatically):
  call cursor(1, 14)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(-1)
Expect:
               G#m7

Given (transpose chord wraps B -> C):
  Bm

Execute (transpose chord wraps B -> C):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  Cm

Given (transpose chord wraps C -> B (down)):
  C

Execute (transpose chord wraps C -> B (down)):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(-1)
Expect:
  B

Given (transpose chord with sharp root):
  C#maj7

Execute (transpose chord with sharp root):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  Dmaj7

Given (no-op on non-chord text):
  hello world

Execute (no-op on non-chord text):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  hello world

Given (a word starting with a chord letter is not a chord):
  Bad

Execute (a word starting with a chord letter is not a chord):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  Bad

Given (a chord root must start the token):
  xAm

Execute (a chord root must start the token):
  call cursor(1, 2)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  xAm

Given (a slash chord transposes as a whole, with the cursor on the bass):
  D/F#

Execute (a slash chord transposes as a whole, with the cursor on the bass):
  call cursor(1, 3)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(1)
Expect:
  D#/G

Given (TransposeChord moves by the given number of semitones):
  Am

Execute (TransposeChord moves by the given number of semitones):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  call songwriter#chord#TransposeChord(-3)
Expect:
  F#m

Given songwriter (<C-A> on a number off a chord is native increment):
  verse 2

Execute (<C-A> on a number off a chord is native increment):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  execute "normal \<C-A>"
Expect:
  verse 3

Given songwriter (<C-X> with a count is native decrement off a chord):
  repeat x10

Execute (<C-X> with a count is native decrement off a chord):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  execute "normal 4\<C-X>"
Expect:
  repeat x6

Given songwriter (<C-A> with a count transposes a chord by that many semitones):
  Am

Execute (<C-A> with a count transposes a chord by that many semitones):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  execute "normal 2\<C-A>"
Expect:
  Bm

Given songwriter (<C-A> on a tab line increments the next fret, not the string name):
  B|--3--|

Execute (<C-A> on a tab line increments the next fret, not the string name):
  call cursor(1, 1)
  execute "normal \<C-A>"
Expect:
  B|--4--|

" Visual <Ctrl-A>/<Ctrl-X>: every chord in the selection is transposed; lines
" without a chord keep Vim's visual increment, frets unsigned on tab lines.

Given songwriter (visual <C-A> transposes every chord of the selected lines):
  Am   G7   D/F#
  Em        C

Execute (visual <C-A> transposes every chord of the selected lines):
  execute "normal ggVj\<C-A>"
Expect songwriter:
  A#m   G#7   D#/G
  Fm        C#

Given songwriter (visual <C-X> with a count transposes down by that many semitones):
  Am   G7

Execute (visual <C-X> with a count transposes down by that many semitones):
  execute "normal V2\<C-X>"
Expect songwriter:
  Gm   F7

Given songwriter (charwise visual <C-A> only transposes the chords it touches):
  Am   G7   D

Execute (charwise visual <C-A> only transposes the chords it touches):
  call cursor(1, 6)
  execute "normal vl\<C-A>"
Expect songwriter:
  Am   G#7   D

Given songwriter (blockwise visual <C-A> transposes the chords in the block):
  Am   G7
  C    D

Execute (blockwise visual <C-A> transposes the chords in the block):
  execute "normal gg\<C-V>j\<C-A>"
Expect songwriter:
  A#m   G7
  C#    D

Given songwriter (visual <C-A> on a tab line increments frets, not as negative numbers):
  e|--3--5--|
  B|--10----|

Execute (visual <C-A> on a tab line increments frets, not as negative numbers):
  " Outside tablature mode, where V is line-wise.
  let b:songwriter_tabmode = 0
  execute "normal ggVj\<C-A>"
Expect songwriter:
  e|--4--5--|
  B|--11----|

Given songwriter (visual <C-A> over chords and prose numbers):
  Am
  verse 2

Execute (visual <C-A> over chords and prose numbers):
  execute "normal ggVj\<C-A>"
Expect songwriter:
  A#m
  verse 3

Given songwriter (visual <C-A> is one undo step and leaves visual mode):
  Am
  e|--3--|

Execute (visual <C-A> is one undo step and leaves visual mode):
  execute "normal ggVj\<C-A>"
  AssertEqual ['A#m', 'e|--4--|'], getline(1, 2)
  AssertEqual 'n', mode()
  AssertEqual [1, 1], [line('.'), col('.')]
  normal u
  AssertEqual ['Am', 'e|--3--|'], getline(1, 2)
